// Flyover Country, version 2: what the dogs say, radio calls and headlines.
//
// leaders   One dog speaks on the morning TV, one line per morning, chosen
//           from the pool that fits the situation.
//             intro, dawn       pure personality. Never mention rules or game words.
//             ahead, behind     how the standings look, in plain words.
//             hit               one of their places got hit. {site} = that place.
//             landed            their raid hit someone. {rival} = who, {site} = where.
//             park, back        off to the secret dog park, and home again with the giant ball.
//             fetch             throwing the giant ball. {site} = the target.
//             win, lose         end of the war.
//           Griffin & Pan lines are tiny dialogues, "Griffin: text | Pan: text",
//           and always start with Griffin.
// radio     Short pilot calls shown as captions during the night (under 80 chars).
//             intercept, jumped {rival} = the other side.
//             hit, miss         {site} = the target.
//             prize             {prize} = Old Faithful, The Boneyard or White Sands.
// headlines The Western Sentinel's front page (under 72 chars).
//             {attacker} {victim} faction short names, {site} place, {prize}, {n} a number.
//
// Tone: affectionate, punch at places and situations, never at people. Nobody
// dies (planes splash, every pilot gets a parachute), the dogs are never in
// danger, no real politics. No colons except in Griffin & Pan dialogue.
FlavorDef(
    leaders: {
        // Princess Donut, Founder & Chief Princess Officer. California.
        "Pacific": LeaderLines(
            intro: [
                "Hello! Princess Donut, founder of the Pacific Venture Republic. I started it in a garage. A nice garage.",
                "Welcome to California, darlings. I'm Princess Donut, and I run all of this from a very sunny office.",
                "I'm Princess Donut. I have big plans for the West, and I've made a slide for every single one.",
                "Hi. Donut. Princess Donut. The tiara is real, the chocolate coat is real, and the vision is very real.",
            ],
            dawn: [
                "Morning! Sunrise walk along the bay, a little sea breeze in my ears, and now I'm ready for anything.",
                "The fog rolled in over the Golden Gate this morning like it was trying to impress me. It worked.",
                "I sat in a sunbeam for twenty minutes and had the nicest think. I've got ideas, darlings.",
                "Today I'm wearing the tiara slightly to the left. It's a whole new direction for the brand.",
                "Palo Alto smells like eucalyptus and ambition this morning. Love that for us.",
                "My assistant says I can't sign things with a paw print. I've signed nine things with a paw print.",
                "There's a new juice bar on University Avenue. I've been three times. They know my order by heart.",
                "The marine layer burned off at ten sharp. I respect a weather system that hits its deadlines.",
                "Small worry. What if the sunshine gets bored of us? No. Look at it out there. It adores us.",
                "I barked at the mail carrier again. He's lovely. It's just something I do. Every founder has a quirk.",
                "I'm proud of all of you. I said so at the all-hands, but I wanted to say it again with my face.",
                "A squirrel outside my window runs the exact same route every morning. I've started cheering for him.",
            ],
            ahead: [
                "We're in the lead, and I'm having my juice delivered with a tiny umbrella in it.",
                "I showed the standings to my investors. They're two cats in the window. They blinked approvingly.",
                "Being out in front suits me. My coat is shinier. I checked in three different mirrors.",
                "We're winning, and I'm so happy the tiara keeps slipping off. I don't even care. Leave it.",
                "Everybody's chasing us now. That's fine. I spent my whole puppyhood being chased. I'm very fast.",
                "We look so good this morning. Quick team photo for the website, please. Chins up, ears up.",
            ],
            behind: [
                "We're behind. I've seen this movie. In the movie, the founder wins. I'm the founder.",
                "Okay, we're trailing. I've cancelled my spa morning. That's how serious I am.",
                "Not where I wanted to be. Every great company has a rough quarter. This is ours, and it's a short one.",
                "We're down a little. I'm doing my thinking walk. It's a fast walk. Try to keep up.",
                "Behind, for now. Someone please bring me a very big whiteboard and a very small snack.",
                "I don't love the standings. I do love this team, which is the part that actually matters.",
            ],
            hit: [
                "Last night somebody hit {site}. I'm upset and I'm not hiding it. Look at my ears. Totally flat.",
                "{site} took a hit. We'll rebuild it faster than anyone thinks. That's sort of our whole thing.",
                "Somebody bombed us while I was asleep. I was having a lovely dream about a launch party, too.",
                "I visited {site} this morning. Everyone's fine. The building is less fine. We'll have it back by Friday.",
                "We got hit last night. I'd like a blanket and five quiet minutes. Then we rebuild.",
                "I'm adding {site} to my list of things to be dramatic about today. It's right at the top.",
            ],
            landed: [
                "Our crews reached {site} last night. Quick, clean, home before sunrise. I'm so proud of them.",
                "We hit {rival} last night and I've been doing little zoomies around the office ever since.",
                "{site} got the full California treatment. Fast, bright, and over before anyone found their slippers.",
                "Last night went exactly to plan, which never happens, so I'm writing it down in my good notebook.",
                "Hello, {rival}. That was us. We wanted to introduce ourselves properly.",
                "Found {site} in the dark on the first try. Everybody on that flight gets a long weekend.",
            ],
            park: [
                "We're taking tonight off at the secret dog park. I need a reset. We all need a reset. Bring snacks.",
                "Tonight we go somewhere nobody can bother us. A dog park. A secret one. I'm so excited I could sneeze.",
                "We're stepping away for one night. Not quitting. Stretching. There's a difference and it involves a pond.",
                "Going dark tonight, darlings. If anyone needs me, I'll be at a pond with my tiara off. Tell no one.",
            ],
            back: [
                "We're back, I feel brand new, and we brought home a tennis ball you can see from space. Don't ask how.",
                "Best night's sleep I've had all year. And now, the big reveal. It's a ball. It's very, very big.",
                "Fully rested, coat brushed, tiara straight. The giant ball is ready whenever I am.",
                "I spent all night at the dog park thinking about one thing. Throwing. Today we throw.",
            ],
            fetch: [
                "This is the launch I've been waiting for. Next stop, {site}. Ready, set, launch!",
                "Everybody watch. I've rehearsed this demo for days. Here it comes, {site}!",
                "I have never wanted to throw anything more in my life. Sorry, {site}. A little sorry.",
                "Tail up, eyes on {site}, and... throw! Oh, it's beautiful. Look at it go.",
            ],
            win: [
                "We won! I'm going to cry a little, and then I'm buying juice for the entire West.",
                "First place. I knew it on day one. I wrote it on a napkin, and now the napkin is framed.",
                "Thank you, team. Really. I'm the one in the tiara, but you're the ones who did it.",
                "We won! Somebody open the sunroof. I'm putting my head out of it and I'm not taking questions.",
            ],
            lose: [
                "That was really well done, winners. Honestly. I'm taking notes for next time.",
                "We didn't win this one. Group nuzzle, everyone. Come on, get in here.",
                "Well played, everyone. I'm going to lie in a sunbeam and think about what I'd do differently.",
                "We lost, and I'm alright with it. Now I have a story for the next founders' dinner.",
            ],
        ),

        // Ranger Huckleberry, Chief Ranger. Washington and Oregon.
        "Cascadia": LeaderLines(
            intro: [
                "Hello. I'm Ranger Huckleberry, Chief Ranger of the Cascadian Commonwealth. Wipe your paws and come in.",
                "Huckleberry here. I look after the forests, the rivers, and anybody who gets lost in them. Welcome.",
                "Morning, or evening. Hard to tell under these clouds. Ranger Huckleberry, at your service.",
                "I'm Huckleberry. Big dog, small hat. I've been a ranger since I was a puppy in a very large raincoat.",
            ],
            dawn: [
                "Coffee's on. Rain's on too. They go well together.",
                "Saw an elk on the drive in. We nodded at each other. Good way to start a day.",
                "There's moss growing on my hat again. I've decided to let it stay. It's earned the spot.",
                "Mount Rainier came out from behind the clouds for about four minutes. Everybody stopped to look.",
                "The river's high and loud this morning. I could listen to it all day, and some days I do.",
                "Shook off on the porch, walked back out into the rain, got wet again. That's the cycle up here.",
                "It's a soft rain today. The kind you barely notice until your ears are full of it.",
                "The Portland farmers market opens at nine. I'll be at the blackberry stand if you need me.",
                "The salmon are running. Nobody tell the bears. Actually, the bears already know.",
                "Did a long hike before sunrise. No reason. Just checking the mountains were all still there.",
                "Sat on the dock and watched the ferry come in. Some mornings don't need anything else.",
                "My slicker has a hole in the left pocket. I keep putting biscuits in it anyway. Hope springs eternal.",
            ],
            ahead: [
                "We're out ahead. Let's keep our voices down and our boots dry.",
                "Things are going well. I'm going to celebrate by standing very still in the rain for a while.",
                "We're leading. Steady pace. The ones who sprint up the switchbacks are the ones who sit down halfway.",
                "Out in front. I like the view from here, but I've learned not to get too attached to a view.",
                "We're ahead, so I put on the good coffee this morning. The one from the little roaster in Olympia.",
                "Good position. Keep doing what you're doing. Quietly, like you're tiptoeing past a sleeping bear.",
            ],
            behind: [
                "We're behind. That's alright. Every trail has an uphill part, and we're in it.",
                "Not our best stretch. Let's dry off, warm up, and get moving again.",
                "We're trailing. I've been lost in the woods before. You don't panic. You find the creek and follow it.",
                "Rough patch. Those cedars took three hundred years to get tall. We've got a few more nights than that.",
                "We're behind and it's raining. Honestly, that's just a Tuesday around here.",
                "We'll catch up. Newfoundlands aren't fast, but we don't get tired, and we're very good swimmers.",
            ],
            hit: [
                "Crews have been out at {site} since dawn in their rain gear. Nobody's hurt. We'll put it right.",
                "I walked through {site} at first light. It's a mess, but it's a mess we know how to clean up.",
                "We took a hit overnight. I made a big pot of coffee for the repair crews. That's step one.",
                "{site} got hit. Whoever did it should know I'm disappointed, and that I have a very long memory.",
                "Rough night. I'm going to take my hat off for a minute and think. Then we get to work.",
                "Somebody hit {site}. Leave no trace, I always say. They did not leave no trace.",
            ],
            landed: [
                "Our crews found {site} through the clouds last night. Steady work. Proud of them.",
                "We paid {rival} a visit. Quiet in, quiet out. The way we like it.",
                "Hit {site} and everyone came home dry. Well, damp. It's still Cascadia.",
                "Good night's work. I won't make a fuss about it. Maybe one small wag.",
                "Sorry, {rival}. We don't usually go out of our way. Last night we went out of our way.",
                "I told the crews headed for {site} to be careful, and they were. Careful, and very effective.",
            ],
            park: [
                "We're spending tonight at the secret dog park down at Four Corners. It's dry there. I hear that's nice.",
                "Even rangers need a night off. Tonight we rest somewhere quiet, with a pond.",
                "Off to the dog park tonight. I've packed a thermos, a towel, and a second towel.",
                "We're stepping off the trail for one night. Sometimes the smart move is to sit down by the water.",
            ],
            back: [
                "Slept like a log. A big, shaggy log. And we've come home with an enormous tennis ball.",
                "Good morning. We're rested, we're dry for once, and we've got one very large ball to throw.",
                "That pond was lovely. I swam for hours. Now, we have a tennis ball the size of a ranger station.",
            ],
            fetch: [
                "I don't usually throw things. Today I'm making an exception. Look out below, {site}.",
                "Steady paws. Deep breath. Ball's away, headed for {site}.",
                "Ranger's honor, I'll pick it up afterward. Throwing now.",
                "It's going to roll a long way. Let's hope it rolls toward {site}. Throw!",
            ],
            win: [
                "We won. Somebody put the big kettle on. Everybody's invited, even the ones who gave us trouble.",
                "Victory. Thank you all for being patient. Patience is a ranger's whole job, and it paid off.",
                "We did it. Slow and steady, wet and steady. Everybody take tomorrow off. Go for a hike.",
                "We won the whole thing. I'm going to sit down now. Newfoundlands sit down very slowly.",
            ],
            lose: [
                "Congratulations to the winners. Well earned. Drive safe on the way home, the roads are slick.",
                "We came up short. The forest doesn't keep score, and I won't either.",
                "Good game, everyone. Let's all head down to the lodge and get warm. Winners go first.",
                "Not our year. The mountains will still be there next time. So will we.",
            ],
        ),

        // Griffin & Pan, Co-Commanders (Brothers). Colorado.
        // Griffin is speckled and watches everything; Pan is bigger, black, and fond of snacks and naps.
        "FrontRange": LeaderLines(
            intro: [
                "Griffin: I'm Griffin. This is my brother Pan. We run Colorado together. | Pan: Hi. Is that a sandwich?",
                "Griffin: Welcome to the Front Range Free State! | Pan: We have mountains. | Griffin: So many mountains.",
                "Griffin: Co-commanders, Front Range Free State. | Pan: He's the speckled one. I'm the handsome one.",
                "Griffin: I'll be watching everything, all the time. | Pan: And I'll be right next to him. Lying down.",
            ],
            dawn: [
                "Griffin: Sunrise over the Rockies. Look at that. | Pan: I'm looking. It's nice. Can we go in now?",
                "Griffin: A magpie has been staring at me for an hour. | Pan: Stare back. | Griffin: I am. It's a standoff.",
                "Griffin: First snow on Longs Peak. | Pan: First fire in the fireplace. | Griffin: Okay, I love that too.",
                "Griffin: You slept on my bed again. | Pan: It was cold, and it smells like you. | Griffin: Oh. Okay.",
                "Griffin: I heard a noise at four in the morning. | Pan: That was me. Getting a drink of water.",
                "Griffin: Did you see the elk on the golf course? | Pan: I saw the elk eat the golf course.",
                "Griffin: The air's so thin up here. | Pan: That's why I take it slow. Altitude. | Griffin: Sure.",
                "Griffin: Where's my breakfast burrito? | Pan: What burrito? | Griffin: Pan. | Pan: It was very good.",
                "Griffin: Three hundred days of sunshine a year. | Pan: And I'm going to nap in every one of them.",
                "Griffin: Wind's coming off the mountains hard today. | Pan: Ears inside out again? | Griffin: Both.",
                "Griffin: Sorry, did my pacing wake you? | Pan: No. I like hearing you walk around. Means you're home.",
                "Griffin: Somebody's roasting green chiles down the street. | Pan: I know. I've known for an hour.",
                "Griffin: I counted the stars last night. | Pan: All of them? | Griffin: Most. You fell asleep on my tail.",
            ],
            ahead: [
                "Griffin: We're out in front! | Pan: Is that good? | Griffin: It's great! | Pan: Then I'm proud of us.",
                "Griffin: We're winning! | Pan: Then I'm taking the big pillow. | Griffin: You always take the big pillow.",
                "Griffin: We're ahead and I still can't relax. | Pan: Lie down for one minute. | Griffin: ...Okay. One.",
                "Griffin: Everybody's looking up at Colorado. | Pan: Because of the mountains? | Griffin: Not today.",
                "Griffin: Why are you rolling in the grass? | Pan: We're winning. Victory roll. | Griffin: Can I do one?",
                "Griffin: I said we'd be ahead by now. | Pan: You say it every night. Tonight you were right.",
            ],
            behind: [
                "Griffin: We're behind. I'm worried. | Pan: I'm not. | Griffin: Why not? | Pan: Because you're on it.",
                "Griffin: We've got ground to make up. | Pan: I'm always behind on walks. You're faster. I still get there.",
                "Griffin: We're losing ground. | Pan: Then we dig in. I'm very good at digging. Ask the yard.",
                "Griffin: Everybody's ahead of us. | Pan: Good. Now they can't see us coming.",
                "Griffin: I barely slept. | Pan: I slept enough for both of us. Here, borrow some. Lean on me.",
                "Griffin: This is bad. | Pan: I'll skip breakfast. | Griffin: Really? | Pan: No. But I thought about it.",
            ],
            hit: [
                "Griffin: They hit {site}! I saw them coming. | Pan: You did. You barked all night. Good barking.",
                "Griffin: Did you feel that? That was {site}. | Pan: That's what shook the couch? Rude. Let's go fix it.",
                "Griffin: {site} took a hit. | Pan: Is everyone okay? | Griffin: Everyone's fine. | Pan: Then we're fine.",
                "Griffin: Somebody hit us last night. | Pan: Want me to go sit on them? | Griffin: Maybe later.",
                "Griffin: I'm so mad about {site}. | Pan: Me too. | Griffin: You're eating. | Pan: I eat when I'm mad.",
                "Griffin: They got past me last night. | Pan: They got past both of us. We're a team. Come here.",
            ],
            landed: [
                "Griffin: Our crews hit {site} right on the dot! | Pan: Of course they did. They learned from you.",
                "Griffin: We got {rival} last night! | Pan: I heard. You did the happy tippy-taps on the kitchen floor.",
                "Griffin: We hit {site}! | Pan: So we won the night? | Griffin: We won the night. | Pan: Tell me again.",
                "Griffin: {rival} never saw us coming. | Pan: Nobody sees us coming. We're very quiet. Except you.",
                "Griffin: Clean hit, and everybody's home. | Pan: Everybody home is my favorite part.",
                "Griffin: I planned that one for two nights. | Pan: I know. I helped. I sat on the map.",
            ],
            park: [
                "Griffin: Secret dog park tonight. | Pan: The one with the pond? | Griffin: The one with the pond.",
                "Griffin: One night off. Just one. | Pan: I'm bringing my blanket. | Griffin: I'll carry it for you.",
                "Griffin: Four Corners is close. We can be there by dark. | Pan: Can we stop for snacks on the way?",
                "Griffin: I won't look at the sky all night. | Pan: Promise? | Griffin: I'll mostly promise.",
            ],
            back: [
                "Griffin: We're back and I feel great! | Pan: You look great. Your ears are all fluffy again.",
                "Griffin: Look what we brought home! | Pan: A tennis ball as big as Denver. | Griffin: Best souvenir ever.",
                "Griffin: The giant ball's loaded and ready. | Pan: Can I hold it first? | Griffin: It's bigger than the house.",
                "Griffin: I slept eight hours! | Pan: I'm so proud of you. | Griffin: And there's a giant ball now!",
            ],
            fetch: [
                "Griffin: Lining up on {site}. | Pan: I'll wiggle for luck. | Griffin: Throw!",
                "Griffin: We throw it together, on three. | Pan: Three! | Griffin: Pan, I hadn't started counting.",
                "Griffin: It's going toward {site}! | Pan: I want to chase it so bad. | Griffin: Me too. Stay. Stay.",
                "Griffin: Big ball, big throw, right at {site}. | Pan: That's my brother. Look at that arm.",
            ],
            win: [
                "Griffin: We won! We actually won! | Pan: I knew you'd do it. | Griffin: We did it. Both of us.",
                "Griffin: We won the whole West. | Pan: Nap? | Griffin: Yeah. Nap. Scoot over.",
                "Griffin: I'm going to read about it all night. | Pan: I'll read it with you. Out loud. I'll do the voices.",
                "Griffin: Colorado wins! | Pan: Pizza for the whole mountain! | Griffin: Pan, that's a lot of pizza.",
            ],
            lose: [
                "Griffin: We lost. I'm sorry, Pan. | Pan: Don't be. You were great. Want half my biscuit?",
                "Griffin: Good game, everybody. You earned it. | Pan: And thank you to whoever made the snacks.",
                "Griffin: We'll get them next time. | Pan: Next time. And I'll stay awake for some of it.",
                "Griffin: We lost. | Pan: Still got the mountains. | Griffin: Still got the couch. | Pan: Still got you.",
            ],
        ),

        // Coach Tank, Head Coach. Texas.
        "Texas": LeaderLines(
            intro: [
                "Coach Tank, Republic of Texas. Bring it in, everybody. Hands in the middle. There we go.",
                "Name's Tank. I coach. I've coached this state since it was a peewee league, and look at it now.",
                "Howdy. Coach Tank. Glad to have you on the team. Hat on, laces tight, let's get to work.",
                "I'm Coach Tank. Blue Lacy, born and raised in the Hill Country. I holler because I care.",
            ],
            dawn: [
                "Morning! Sun's up over Austin, the tacos are hot and I've got my whistle. That's everything I need.",
                "Took the long way in this morning. Texas is mostly long ways. Bluebonnets the whole drive.",
                "Watched some old game tape last night. Fell asleep halfway and woke up with the remote on my ear.",
                "Got a breakfast taco in each paw. Don't tell the trainer.",
                "Big sky today. I know, it's big every day. Today it's showing off.",
                "Saw a kid throw a perfect spiral in the park this morning. I gave him a nod. He nodded back.",
                "Cicadas started buzzing before sunrise. Loudest marching band in Texas. I kind of love 'em.",
                "I want y'all to know I'm proud of how you carry yourselves. Shoulders back. That's Texas.",
                "Stopped at a gas station the size of a small town. Bought jerky. Went back in for more jerky.",
                "A thunderstorm rolled through at dawn. I sat on the porch and watched it like a championship game.",
                "Fixed the screen door this morning. Nothing better than a job done right. Remember that.",
                "Friday night lights, Saturday morning brisket. I'd live in that weekend forever if they let me.",
            ],
            ahead: [
                "We're up! Don't dance in the end zone. Hand the ball to the ref like you've been there before.",
                "Look at that lead. That's what happens when you do the boring stuff right every single day.",
                "We're ahead. Good. Now we play like we're behind. Nobody gets comfy on my sideline.",
                "Out in front, playing clean, and nobody's whining. That's a team. That's my team.",
                "We're winning, and the whole state's walking a little taller this morning. Even the cattle.",
                "I'm grinning so wide my whistle fell out. Keep it rolling, team.",
            ],
            behind: [
                "We're down. Fine. Nobody remembers the first half. They remember the comeback.",
                "Behind on the board. I've been drawing up new plays since four this morning. Got some good ones.",
                "We're trailing, and I'm not worried. I've watched y'all practice. I know what's in there.",
                "Down a few. Tighten the chin straps and play our kind of football.",
                "Scoreboard's not pretty this morning. Good thing we never played for pretty.",
                "We're behind, so everybody's counting us out. That's my favorite thing in the whole world.",
            ],
            hit: [
                "They hit {site} last night. Alright. Get the crews out there, and we'll study the tape later.",
                "{site} took one on the chin. Texas has a big chin. We'll be fine.",
                "Somebody snuck one past our line last night. That won't happen twice, I promise you.",
                "Folks at {site} were already sweeping up when I got there. Didn't even have to ask 'em.",
                "We took a hit. Happens to the best teams. What matters is the next snap.",
                "{site} got rattled. I'm not mad, son. I'm motivated. There's a difference, and you're about to see it.",
            ],
            landed: [
                "We hit {rival} right on the money. Game ball goes to every crew that flew.",
                "{site} got a visit from Texas last night. Clean execution. Textbook, son.",
                "Beautiful work last night. Y'all made an old coach very happy.",
                "Hey, {rival}, sorry about {site}. Not that sorry. It was a heck of a play.",
                "Ran it exactly like we ran it in practice. That's all I ever ask of anybody.",
                "That run at {site} was the prettiest play I've seen all season.",
            ],
            park: [
                "We're calling a timeout. One night at the secret dog park. Rest up, son.",
                "Locker room's at Four Corners tonight. Grass, water, and nobody yelling. Except me, a little.",
                "Even champions take a knee sometimes. Tonight we take it at the dog park.",
                "Everybody to the bench. We're going to roll around in some grass and come back hungry.",
            ],
            back: [
                "Back from the break with fresh legs and a tennis ball the size of a stadium. Let's play ball.",
                "Best halftime we ever had. Everybody's rested, and we've got one big trick play loaded up.",
                "We're back on the field. Feel that? That's what a good night's sleep does for a team.",
                "Look at the size of that ball. I've waited my whole career to throw something like that.",
            ],
            fetch: [
                "Drops back, looks downfield, sees {site} wide open. Lets it fly!",
                "Go deep, ball! All the way to {site}!",
                "This is the play we've been saving. Everybody watch. Here it goes.",
                "Biggest throw in Texas history, and we've had some big ones. Heads up, {site}!",
            ],
            win: [
                "We won it all! I'm hollering so loud they can hear me in Oklahoma.",
                "Champions of the West. I've never been prouder of a team. Not ever.",
                "We won! Practice is cancelled tomorrow. And the day after. Go see your mamas.",
                "The trophy's coming home to Austin. Polish it up and put it somewhere big. Everything here is big.",
            ],
            lose: [
                "Good game, everybody. Line up, shake hands, look 'em in the eye. That's how Texas loses.",
                "Season's over. Hold your heads up on the bus home. You earned that much.",
                "They beat us fair. Tip your caps. Then go get some rest. We start again Monday.",
                "Didn't go our way. I've lost before and I'll coach again tomorrow. Love you, team.",
            ],
        ),

        // Lucky, Pit Boss. Nevada.
        "Dreamland": LeaderLines(
            intro: [
                "Morning. Or evening. In Vegas it's hard to tell. I'm Lucky, Pit Boss of the Dreamland Syndicate.",
                "Lucky's the name. Pug, visor, bow tie. Pull up a stool, friend. Coffee's fresh.",
                "Welcome to Nevada. I'm Lucky. I'd show you the whole desert, but some of it doesn't exist.",
                "I'm Lucky. I've worked every table on the Strip and I have never once missed a buffet.",
            ],
            dawn: [
                "The neon's still buzzing from last night. I like to watch it switch off when the sun comes up.",
                "Desert's quiet this early. Just me, a coffee and a roadrunner who keeps looking at me funny.",
                "There were lights out past Rachel again last night. Weather balloons. Very fast weather balloons.",
                "The breakfast buffet opens at six. I'm there at five fifty-nine. That's professionalism.",
                "My bow tie has been crooked since 1998. I've decided that's on purpose.",
                "Ninety-eight degrees and it's not even breakfast. Dry heat, though. Everybody says dry heat.",
                "Somebody hit a jackpot downtown last night. I heard the bells from my bed. Happy for 'em.",
                "I snore. The whole Strip knows I snore. It's a pug thing. We don't talk about it.",
                "Took a stroll down Fremont Street. A guy dressed as Elvis gave me half his sandwich. Classy guy.",
                "I counted the chips twice this morning. They're all there. They're always all there. I count anyway.",
                "Hot tip. Don't walk on the pavement after ten. Ask my paws how I know.",
                "Red Rock looks real pretty this morning. Sometimes I forget there's a whole world outside the casino.",
            ],
            ahead: [
                "We're up. I'm not saying a word about it. You don't talk about a hot streak. You just nod.",
                "Look at that stack of chips. I could build a little fort. I might.",
                "The odds are with us this morning. They called ahead to say so.",
                "We're ahead, and I'm in such a good mood I tipped the valet twice.",
                "I knew we'd be out in front. I had a feeling. Pugs have very good feelings.",
                "Good morning, high rollers. We're ahead. Keep your hands steady and your chips right where they are.",
            ],
            behind: [
                "We're down a few chips. A smart player knows the difference between a long night and a lost one.",
                "Cold dice this week. I'm blowing on them. I'm a pug, so it's mostly snorting, but still.",
                "Behind. Fine. I've seen guys come back from worse at the craps table. I've seen it twice.",
                "Not our week. I'm switching to my backup bow tie. The polka dot one. It knows what it did.",
                "We're behind, and everybody's betting against us. I love long odds. They pay better.",
                "The house is having an off night. It happens. Even the fountains take a break sometimes.",
            ],
            hit: [
                "{site} got hit, so somebody's banned from every buffet in Nevada. Effective immediately.",
                "I'm comping the repair crews at {site} whatever they want. Within reason.",
                "Rule one in this town, never look rattled after a bad night. Is my visor straight? Good.",
                "I'm smiling about {site}, because that's the job. Under the visor, I'm not smiling.",
                "Rough night. The lights flickered on the Strip. Everybody kept playing. That's Vegas.",
                "I saw the pictures from {site}. Bad luck. But bad luck turns. That's the one thing I know for sure.",
            ],
            landed: [
                "We hit {site} last night. The house sends its regards.",
                "{rival} sat down at our table and lost a hand. Nothing personal. That's the game.",
                "Good work out there. Everybody gets a comp. Everybody gets two comps.",
                "Our flyers came out of the desert and found {site}. They won't say how. Very discreet bunch.",
                "Hey, {rival}. No hard feelings. Come out to the Strip sometime, I'll get you a nice room.",
                "Clean night. In and out before the dealers changed shifts. Like we were never there.",
            ],
            park: [
                "We're cashing out for one night. Got a quiet place at Four Corners. Pond, grass, no slot machines.",
                "Tonight the pit boss takes a break. I'll be at a dog park nobody knows about. Well, almost nobody.",
                "Closing the tables for the night. Even this town sleeps sometimes. Not often. Tonight.",
                "Walking away from the table for one night. Smart players know when.",
            ],
            back: [
                "We're back, rested, and holding a tennis ball the size of a casino. Let's play.",
                "Slept like a champ. Snored like one too. Now we're holding the biggest chip in the West.",
                "The house is open again. Fresh coffee, fresh dealers, and a ball you won't believe.",
                "Good morning. I came back from that dog park with a secret. It's round, and it's enormous.",
            ],
            fetch: [
                "Biggest bet I've ever placed, and I'm placing it on {site}. Roll 'em!",
                "Dealer's calling it. Ball goes to {site}. Everybody watch.",
                "Thirty years in this business and I've never held a hand like this one. Throwing!",
                "Odds on this one are very, very good. {site} just became a long shot.",
            ],
            win: [
                "We won. Pool's open, rooms with a view for everybody. It's all on the house tonight.",
                "Top of the board. Don't ask me how I called it. Some of that's classified.",
                "We won the West! Turn on every light on the Strip. All of 'em. At once.",
                "Victory. I'm going to sit in the good chair and let the whole city rub my belly.",
            ],
            lose: [
                "Good game, friends. You beat the house fair and square. Come back anytime.",
                "We lost. Happens to everybody in this town eventually. I'm buying the winners breakfast.",
                "Congrats to the winners. The fountains on the Strip are on me tonight. Go make a wish.",
                "Not our night. But in this town, there's always another night.",
            ],
        ),

        // Agent Sorghum, County Extension Agent. North Dakota to Oklahoma.
        "GrainBelt": LeaderLines(
            intro: [
                "Agent Sorghum, County Extension. I cover a lot of ground for a corgi. Pleased to meet you.",
                "Morning. Sorghum's the name. If it grows between Fargo and Oklahoma City, I've got opinions on it.",
                "I'm Agent Sorghum with the Grain Belt Union. Wipe your boots, sit a spell, coffee's in the thermos.",
                "Hello there. Sorghum. Short legs, long fields. We make it work.",
            ],
            dawn: [
                "Sun came up flat and orange over the wheat. Same as yesterday. I never get tired of it.",
                "The combine's making a noise I don't like. I've decided to stare at it until it stops.",
                "County fair's next week. I'm judging zucchini again. Folks always grow 'em too big.",
                "Meadowlark on the fence post this morning sang the whole song, start to finish. Good sign.",
                "Wind's out of the south at twenty. That's a calm day in Kansas. Hold onto your hat.",
                "Dug a hole in the test plot this morning. For soil sampling. Mostly for soil sampling.",
                "Coffee at the co-op, then over to look at the Andersons' sunflowers. Busy morning.",
                "Rain's coming. I can smell it, and my knee's been telling me since Tuesday.",
                "Saw a thunderhead out west that must've been ten miles tall. Pretty, from a distance.",
                "I herded the neighbor's ducks into a nice tight group this morning. Nobody asked. It just felt right.",
                "Somebody brought kolaches to the extension office. I won't say who. It was me.",
                "Got a postcard from the Ball of Twine folks. They added another layer this summer. Doing great.",
                "Sky's so big out here this morning you could lose a whole afternoon looking at it.",
            ],
            ahead: [
                "We're out ahead. Good. Now's when you check the fences, not when you put your feet up.",
                "Things are going our way. I'll take it like I take a good rain. Gratefully, and without fuss.",
                "Leading the West. My grandpa would've called that a fine crop. Then gone right back to work.",
                "We're ahead, and I'm so pleased my whole back end is wagging. Corgis wag from the back end.",
                "We're ahead. Took a lot of slow, plain, boring work to get here. Boring work is the best work.",
                "Out in front. Don't brag down at the co-op. Let 'em figure it out on their own.",
            ],
            behind: [
                "We're behind. Planted late, that's all. Late crops still come in.",
                "Not the season we wanted. I've seen plenty of those. You keep at it.",
                "We're trailing. My mother always said dig in, stay low, and keep moving. Never failed her.",
                "Behind, for now. A field looks like nothing for weeks, then one morning it's all green.",
                "We're down. Worrying never brought rain to a single field, so I'm not going to bother.",
                "Bit of a dry spell. That's the plains. You wait it out, then you work twice as hard.",
            ],
            hit: [
                "We've rebuilt after hail, wind and one very confused tornado. We'll rebuild {site} too.",
                "{site} took a beating. I've got my clipboard out and I'm writing it all down.",
                "Somebody hit us overnight. Didn't even close the gate behind 'em.",
                "Drove out to {site} at dawn. Neighbors were already showing up with coffee and toolboxes.",
                "Took a hit last night. Out here, when somebody falls down, you help 'em up. That's what we're doing.",
                "I'm not one to get worked up. But {site}? Somebody's getting a very stern look from a corgi.",
            ],
            landed: [
                "Flew low over the fields to {site} and right back home. Good, quiet work.",
                "{rival} had a long night. We had a good one. Sorry, neighbor.",
                "Good work, crews. Steady, careful and right on the mark, like planting a straight row.",
                "Hit {site}. I don't like to crow about it. I'll leave that to the roosters.",
                "Our crews flew all night to reach {rival}. Long way. Flat, though. Easy to find.",
                "Last night went right, start to finish. Thank you to the crews and the weather, in that order.",
            ],
            park: [
                "Even good soil needs a rest. Tonight we're off to the dog park out by Four Corners.",
                "Heading out to the secret dog park. Long drive. I've packed sandwiches.",
                "One night off. Let the field sit, let the crews sleep. It'll all be here tomorrow.",
                "I'll be by the pond tonight, under the cottonwood, not thinking about a single thing.",
            ],
            back: [
                "Back home with fresh crews and a tennis ball as big as a grain elevator. Never seen the like.",
                "Rested up, fed up, and ready. Well, not fed up. Well fed. You know what I mean.",
                "Morning. We're back, and there's something big and fuzzy strapped to the hay trailer.",
            ],
            fetch: [
                "Checked the wind, checked the angle. Here she goes, {site}.",
                "Biggest thing ever thrown on the plains, and it's headed straight for {site}.",
                "Short legs, strong arm. Throwing!",
                "That ball's going to roll clear across three counties. Throwing it now.",
            ],
            win: [
                "We won. Feels like the last load of the harvest coming in. Tired, happy, proud.",
                "Victory for the Grain Belt. Everybody out to the fairgrounds. There's a cake shaped like a tractor.",
                "That's the season. I'm going to go lie in a wheat field and look at the sky for a while.",
                "Thank you, everyone. Good teams are like good soil. Takes years. Worth every one.",
            ],
            lose: [
                "Good season for the winners. Real good. Tip of the seed cap to you.",
                "That's farming. Some seasons you lose. You learn something, and you plant again.",
                "Lost this one. The neighbors are still the neighbors, though, and that's what counts.",
                "Good game, all. If you're ever in Lincoln, I'll show you the best diner in the state.",
            ],
        ),

        // Biscuit, Chief Volunteer. Utah.
        "Beehive": LeaderLines(
            intro: [
                "Hi! I'm Biscuit, Chief Volunteer of the Beehive Cooperative. I'm so glad you're here. Really!",
                "Oh my heck, hello! I'm Biscuit. I brought a casserole. I always bring a casserole.",
                "Hello! I'm Biscuit. That's what my name tag says, and I'd never wear a name tag that fibbed.",
                "Welcome to Utah! I'm Biscuit. If you need anything at all, I'm probably already on my way.",
            ],
            dawn: [
                "Good morning! I got here at five to set up the chairs. Nobody needed chairs. They look very neat.",
                "Fresh powder up Little Cottonwood! Greatest Snow on Earth. It says so right on the license plates.",
                "I made green Jell-O with shredded carrots in it. People keep calling it interesting. Thank you!",
                "The sunrise on the Wasatch this morning! Pink, then gold. I just stood there wagging.",
                "Somebody parked crooked at the grocery store. I left a little note that said have a wonderful day.",
                "Today's plan is help a neighbor move a couch, get a dirty soda, then help another neighbor move a couch.",
                "Drove down to Bryce Canyon last weekend. Those hoodoos made me feel small, and I'm a pretty big dog.",
                "I'm sorry I'm so early. I'm always early. I once showed up first to my own surprise party.",
                "My tie has little honeybees on it today. It's my fancy tie. No reason. I just felt fancy.",
                "Took a walk by the Great Salt Lake. It smells a little funny, but it means well.",
                "The fry sauce at the drive-in was perfect this morning. I asked for extra and they said of course.",
                "A family of quail crossed the road in front of me. I stopped and waited. They seemed to appreciate it.",
                "Gosh, I love a potluck. Seven kinds of potatoes and nobody has to choose.",
            ],
            ahead: [
                "We're ahead! Oh my heck. I'm trying to be humble about it. I'm wagging way too hard to be humble.",
                "Look at that, out in front! I made a little banner. It's crooked, but it's from the heart.",
                "We're leading, so I baked cookies for everyone. Including the folks who aren't. Especially them.",
                "Things are going really well! Let's be extra kind today. It's easy to be kind when you're ahead.",
                "We're in front! I called my mom. She said that's nice, dear, are you wearing a coat?",
                "We're winning. I'm going to go sit quietly in the car for a minute and smile.",
            ],
            behind: [
                "We're behind, but that's okay! Hard work fixes almost everything. Sandwiches fix the rest.",
                "Tough couple of nights. I made a list of ways to do better. It's two pages, front and back.",
                "Flip. We're trailing. Okay! We'll just get up earlier. I'll set my alarm for... earlier.",
                "I brought everyone hot chocolate this morning. Little things help. We'll catch up!",
                "We're losing. Okay. Deep breath. Roll up the sleeves. They're already short. Great!",
                "We're behind and I'm a little worried. But I've never once given up on a stuck jar lid.",
            ],
            hit: [
                "They hit {site} last night! Oh my heck. Okay. I've already signed up to help clean it up.",
                "Everyone at {site} is safe, thank goodness. I'm bringing casseroles to the crews.",
                "Someone hit us overnight, so I put on my serious tie. It's the plain blue one. It means business.",
                "Gosh, {site}. That was a nice place. It'll be nice again, I promise. Grab a broom!",
                "Rough night. I sat with the crews this morning and we all had pancakes. We'll be okay.",
                "Whoever hit {site}, I hope you slept well. We didn't. But I really do hope you did!",
            ],
            landed: [
                "We reached {site} last night! I gave every crew a little gold star sticker this morning.",
                "The crews flew to {rival} and back and were home right on time. Early, actually. Very punctual.",
                "Last night went great. I'm so proud I could burst. Gently. Politely.",
                "Sorry about {site}, {rival}! Truly. I'll bring over some fry sauce to make up for it.",
                "Good flying, everybody. Clean, careful, and nobody showed off. That's how we like it.",
                "{rival} had a rough night, and I feel a little bad. Mostly I feel proud of our crews!",
            ],
            park: [
                "We're heading to the secret dog park at Four Corners tonight! I'm bringing a cooler and four kinds of chips.",
                "One night off! I've packed a picnic, a frisbee, extra frisbees, and folding chairs for everyone.",
                "Short drive to Four Corners tonight. I'll be the one splashing in the pond. Sorry in advance.",
                "Taking a breather tonight. Even busy bees sit on a flower sometimes.",
            ],
            back: [
                "We're back! Everybody's rested, and there's a tennis ball the size of a ski lodge out back!",
                "What a night. I swam, I napped, I swam again. And now we have the biggest ball I've ever seen.",
                "Good morning! All rested and ready. I polished the giant ball. It didn't need it. I wanted to.",
            ],
            fetch: [
                "Okay! Paws planted, big swing. This one's for {site}. Wheee!",
                "I've wanted to throw something this big my whole life. Here goes!",
                "Heads up, {site}! I mean that nicely. Please, really, heads up.",
                "Wind's good, sky's clear, and my tail's going a hundred miles an hour. Throw!",
            ],
            win: [
                "We won! Oh my heck! Green Jell-O for everyone! I made nine of them. I was hoping.",
                "Thank you, thank you, thank you! I'm going to hug every single person in Utah. Line forms on the left.",
                "We did it! I'm going to go roll in the snow up at Alta for about an hour.",
                "Champions! Fry sauce on everything tonight. Fries, burgers, the cake. Okay, maybe not the cake.",
            ],
            lose: [
                "Congratulations! You played so well. I've wrapped up some leftovers for your drive home.",
                "We didn't win, but I had the best time with all of you. Truly. Same time next year?",
                "Good game, everyone! I'll be honest, I'm a little sad. But mostly I'm happy for you.",
                "Well done to the winners. Here, let me help you carry that trophy to the car.",
            ],
        ),
    },

    radio: {
        "Pacific": Radio(
            intercept: [
